==English==

===Etymology===
{{clipping|en|notext=1}}
[[Appendix:Glossary#clipping|Clippings]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛpoʊ/|/ˈɹiːpoʊ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} {{clipping of|en|repossession|addl=most commonly of a [[vehicle]], [[house]] or [[condominium]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|Can you do a '''repo''' tomorrow? It's an SUV in Springfield.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{clipping of|en|repositioning}}.
#: {{ux|en|That cruise ship starts its '''repo''' tomorrow; it's going to the Caribbean for the winter.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|finance|informal}} {{clipping of|en|repurchase}} A type of agreement which allows a borrower to use a financial [[security]] as [[collateral]] for a cash loan at a fixed interest rate, or to buy something back that was sold.
#* {{RQ:FT|edition=weekend|date=2026-09-05|title=The financial world's ‘dark matter’|author=Robin Wigglesworth|page=18|passage=Simple descriptions of the '''repo''' market make it sound quotidian. It consists of selling assets and agreeing to buy them back at a later date at a slight mark-up.}}
# {{senseid|en|computing}} {{lb|en|countable|computing|informal}} {{clipping of|en|repository||storage location for files}}.
#: {{hypo|en|monorepo}}
#: {{ux|en|I checked out the {{w|Git}} '''repo''' to edit it.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|multirepo|polyrepo|subrepo
|repo depot|repo man|reverse repo}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To [[repossess]].
#: {{ux|en|I had my car '''repoed''' when I became unable to keep up the payments.}}

